::heading level=1 id=rui-project-index
rui — project index
::end

::heading level=2 id=understanding
Understanding
::end

::paragraph id=paragraph-3-2
A caller declares a view by composing elements with the builder API — El::new() chains method calls for children, properties, event handlers. The App frame loop owns the Backend trait's implementation per platform; each tick receives input (pointer, keyboard, window events), drives the layout engine to reflow the tree, queries each Painter for damage, renders deltas, and presents to screen.

The package name is rui-native (the Cargo.toml [package] name), but the library export is still rui (the [lib] name), so dependents must declare it as rui = { package = "rui-native", path = "../../rui" } (console/) or rui-native = { package = "rui-native", path = "../../rui" } (sara-ui/). The WebAssembly backend compiles the same library to rui_bg.wasm; Forge's web UI imports it at web/pkg/rui_bg.wasm and calls it from TypeScript to render a GitHub-like repository interface.

Build (dev): completes in 0.01s when already built. Test suite: 413 passing tests, 0 failures, 0.21s runtime. The architecture is platform-agnostic: the Backend trait abstracts macOS (Cocoa), Windows (Win32), Linux (X11/Wayland), and browser (WebAssembly) rendering. All drawing goes through a Painter API that auto-detects light/dark theme. The charter is pixel-perfect visual parity across all five platforms and production readiness with zero external crates.
::end

::paragraph id=paragraph-2
From the project's own README: A declarative interface library for Rust, with no dependencies at all.
::end

::paragraph id=paragraph-3
Scaffold from the file tree, written by dx index. Improve it: replace each TODO with what the area does and how it connects to the rest, and add code blocks for the load-bearing files — they render as the file's current text, never a stale copy. Files below are ranked by how load-bearing they look (entry points, how many files reference them, size); trust the ranking as a place to start, not as the truth. Keep this document true as the code changes.
::end

::paragraph id=paragraph-4
Direction (2026-08-26): rui is gaining a WebAssembly rendering backend so it can run inside a browser, not just as a native window — see the Now worklist below. The concrete driver is [[Forge]], a self-hosted git server whose web UI (currently plain HTML/CSS/JS) is being rebuilt on rui-wasm into a real GitHub-style UI (repo list, file tree, blob viewer, commit log). SARA's engine watches both this project and Forge (factory/.sara/config.json's watchedProjects) and should treat them as one coordinated initiative — a rui primitive Forge's UI needs belongs in rui's own worklist, not duplicated or worked around in Forge.
::end

